Subject: stars and the sun at infinity in the visionOS 3D mode (D-097)

THE PROBLEM. starsRender() projects every star itself and draws it as a one-
pixel gDPFillRectangle; skyRenderSuns() draws the sun's orb, and
skyRenderArtifacts() the source glare of its lens flare, as texture rectangles
at a screen position sky.c computed (func0f0b2150). None of them has a matrix,
so the stereo fold (0030) never sees them and both eyes drew them in the same
pixels: zero disparity, ON the panel, 7.6 m away - while the sky dome they hang
in is folded skew-only (the SKY class) and sits at infinity. A star field in
front of its own sky.

THE FIX reuses D-060's depth tag. The payload's top value, 0x7fff, now means
INFINITY: the renderer gives such a rectangle the fold's far asymptote
(q = 0 in the glare arithmetic), which is exactly the disparity the sky's
skew-only class gives the dome. The stars take it as a sticky span around
their loop; the sun's orb, and the flare's source glare, as a closed span
around their one rectangle (func0f0b2150 can draw nothing, and a one-rect tag
would then fall on the next rectangle, the HUD's). The flare's six ghosts are
the lens's, not the sky's, and stay on the panel; a teleport's flare opens no
span and is unchanged.

Tags are G_NOOPs under #ifndef PLATFORM_N64: 2D, the macOS oracle's gfx stream
and the N64 build are unchanged. A release (XBLA) sky paints its own stars and
starsRender() is not called under it (bg.c), so this is the N64 sky's star
field.

diff --git a/port/fast3d/gfx_pc.cpp b/port/fast3d/gfx_pc.cpp
index 9e0994f9c..d2ff3e136 100644
--- a/port/fast3d/gfx_pc.cpp
+++ b/port/fast3d/gfx_pc.cpp
@@ -7981,7 +7981,12 @@ static void gfx_draw_rectangle(int32_t ulx, int32_t uly, int32_t lrx, int32_t lr
             pdVisionStereoNearLaw(&worldN, &gunN, &knee);
             const float qm = (1.0f + worldN) / conv;
             const float q0 = (1.0f + worldN * knee) / conv;
-            const float q  = gfx_stereo_soft_q(1.0f / d, q0, qm, qm - q0);
+            // D-097: the payload's top value is INFINITY (stars, the sun):
+            // q = 0, the fold's own far asymptote, which is the disparity the
+            // sky dome gets from its skew-only class.
+            const float q  = (d >= (float)PD_DLTAG_DEPTH_INF)
+                                 ? 0.0f
+                                 : gfx_stereo_soft_q(1.0f / d, q0, qm, qm - q0);
             const float dx = pd_stereo.world_a * eSigned * (1.0f / conv - q);
             ulxf += dx;
             lrxf += dx;
diff --git a/src/game/sky.c b/src/game/sky.c
index bc7cd02e5..b8688ef44 100644
--- a/src/game/sky.c
+++ b/src/game/sky.c
@@ -3630,7 +3630,20 @@ Gfx *skyRenderSuns(Gfx *gdl, bool xray)
 					sp12c[0] *=  SCREEN_ASPECT / videoGetAspect();
 #endif
 
+#ifndef PLATFORM_N64
+					// D-097: the sun's orb at infinity in the visionOS 3D
+					// mode, like the sky it is painted on, instead of ON the
+					// panel. A closed span rather than a one-rect tag:
+					// func0f0b2150 draws nothing for a sprite wholly off the
+					// top or left, and a one-rect tag would then land on
+					// whatever rectangle came next (the HUD's).
+					gDPPdDlTag(gdl++, PD_DLTAG_DEPTH(PD_DLTAG_DEPTH_INF));
+					gDPPdDlTag(gdl++, PD_DLSPAN_DEPTH_BEGIN);
+#endif
 					func0f0b2150(&gdl, sp134, sp12c, g_TexLightGlareConfigs[5].width, g_TexLightGlareConfigs[5].height, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 1);
+#ifndef PLATFORM_N64
+					gDPPdDlTag(gdl++, PD_DLSPAN_DEPTH_END);
+#endif
 
 					gDPPipeSync(gdl++);
 					gDPSetColorDither(gdl++, G_CD_BAYER);
@@ -3727,6 +3740,14 @@ Gfx *skyRenderFlare(Gfx *gdl, f32 x, f32 y, f32 intensityfrac, f32 size, s32 fla
 
 	func0f0b2150(&gdl, sp17c, sp174, g_TexLightGlareConfigs[6].width, g_TexLightGlareConfigs[6].height, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 1);
 
+#ifndef PLATFORM_N64
+	// D-097: the source glare above is the only part of a SUN's flare that
+	// skyRenderArtifacts() opened an infinity span for; the six ghosts below
+	// are the lens's and stay on the panel. A teleport's flare opens no span,
+	// and closing one that is not open is a no-op.
+	gDPPdDlTag(gdl++, PD_DLSPAN_DEPTH_END);
+#endif
+
 	// Render the other artifacts
 	texSelect(&gdl, &g_TexLightGlareConfigs[1], 4, 0, 2, 1, NULL);
 
@@ -3964,6 +3985,12 @@ Gfx *skyRenderArtifacts(Gfx *gdl)
 			f32 intensityfrac = skyGetArtifactGroupIntensityFrac(artifacts);
 
 			if (intensityfrac > 0.0f) {
+#ifndef PLATFORM_N64
+				// D-097: the flare's SOURCE glare sits on the sun, so it is at
+				// infinity too; skyRenderFlare() closes the span after it.
+				gDPPdDlTag(gdl++, PD_DLTAG_DEPTH(PD_DLTAG_DEPTH_INF));
+				gDPPdDlTag(gdl++, PD_DLSPAN_DEPTH_BEGIN);
+#endif
 				gdl = skyRenderFlare(gdl, g_SunScreenXPositions[i], g_SunScreenYPositions[i], intensityfrac, sun->orb_size, g_SunFlareTimers240[i], g_SunAlphaFracs[i]);
 			}
 		}
